RESUME SKILL GAP ANALYZER - JavaScript Implementation Documentation
================================================================

1. OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This document explains the JavaScript implementation for the Resume Skill Gap
Analyzer. The JS handles form validation, file upload, API simulation, and result
display with skeleton loading animations.


2. CONFIGURATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
File: app.js contains configuration constants:

const CONFIG = {
    maxFileSize: 5 * 1024 * 1024,  // 5MB
    allowedFileTypes: ['application/pdf', 'application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document'],
    allowedExtensions: ['.pdf', '.docx'],
    apiDelay: 1500  // 1.5 second simulated API delay
};

- File size limit: 5MB
- Accepted formats: PDF, DOCX
- Simulated response delay: 1.5 seconds


3. JOB CATEGORIES DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
JOB_CATEGORIES object stores all 14 job categories with:

{
    key: {
        name: 'Display Name',
        skills: ['Skill1', 'Skill2', ...],
        icon: 'emoji'
    }
}

Categories:
1. software  - Software Development
2. web      - Web Development
3. mobile   - Mobile Development
4. uiux     - UI/UX Design
5. data     - Data Science
6. aiml     - AI/ML
7. cloud    - Cloud Computing
8. security - Cybersecurity
9. database - Database Engineering
10. devops  - DevOps
11. networking - Networking
12. gaming  - Game Development
13. qa      - QA/Testing
14. pm      - Project Management

Each category contains 10 required skills.


4. UTILITY FUNCTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 showSkeletonLoader()
- Creates overlay with animated skeleton cards
- Dynamically adds CSS styles
- Shows "loading" state during API calls

4.2 hideSkeletonLoader()
- Removes skeleton overlay from DOM

4.3 showError(message, containerId)
- Displays error message in specified container
- Auto-removes after 5 seconds

4.4 simulateApiCall(data, delay)
- Async function simulating API request
- Shows skeleton loader during delay
- Returns success response with timestamp


5. FORM HANDLERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 initLoginForm()
- Handles login form submission
- Basic validation: checks email/password not empty
- Calls simulateApiCall() for auth
- Redirects to dashboard on success

5.2 initRegisterForm()
- Handles registration form submission
- Basic validation: checks name/email/password not empty
- Calls simulateApiCall() for registration
- Redirects to dashboard on success


6. FILE UPLOAD HANDLER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6.1 initFileUpload()
- Handles file input change event
- Processes drag-and-drop events
- Validates file type and size

File Validation:
- Allowed types: application/pdf, application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document
- Allowed extensions: .pdf, .docx
- Max size: 5MB

On Success:
- Adds 'uploaded' class to upload area
- Displays file name
- Enables analyze button


7. CATEGORY SELECTION HANDLER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

7.1 initCategorySelect()
- Listens for category dropdown changes
- Calls loadSkills() when category selected

7.2 loadSkills(category)
- Retrieves skills from JOB_CATEGORIES
- Dynamically creates skill tag elements
- Makes skills clickable for selection
- Stores selected category globally


8. ANALYZE RESUME HANDLER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

8.1 initAnalyzeButton()
- Enables/disables button based on form completion
- Calls analyzeResume() on click

8.2 analyzeResume()
- Collects uploaded file
- Collects selected category and skills
- Stores result in localStorage
- Calls simulateApiCall() with analysis data
- Redirects to result.html on completion


9. RESULT PAGE HANDLER
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

9.1 initResultPage()
- Checks localStorage for analyzeResult
- Redirects to dashboard if no data
- Updates category name in result page


10. INITIALIZATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Page-specific initialization via DOMContentLoaded:

if (path.includes('login.html')) {
    initLoginForm();
} else if (path.includes('register.html')) {
    initRegisterForm();
} else if (path.includes('dashboard.html')) {
    initCategorySelect();
    initFileUpload();
    initAnalyzeButton();
} else if (path.includes('result.html')) {
    initResultPage();
}


11. GLOBAL STORAGE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data stored in browser:

localStorage:
- analyzeResult: JSON string with analysis data
    {
        category: 'software',
        categoryName: 'Software Development',
        skills: ['Java', 'Python', ...],
        timestamp: '2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z'
    }

window global variables:
- window.uploadedFile: File object
- window.selectedCategory: String (category key)


12. ERROR HANDLING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Basic validation errors:
- Empty form fields -> "Please fill in all fields"
- Invalid file type -> "Please upload PDF or DOCX file"
- File too large -> "File size must be less than 5MB"

No backend - all API calls are simulated.


13. SKELETON LOADING ANIMATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Custom CSS dynamically added to page:

.skeleton-overlay - Full screen overlay
.skeleton-card - Loading container
.skeleton-line - Animated text placeholder
.skeleton-box - Animated card placeholder

Animation: shimmer effect using gradient background-position


14. FILE STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
app.js - Main JavaScript file

HTML files include app.js:
- login.html
- register.html
- dashboard.html
- result.html

Each HTML calls appropriate init function on DOMContentLoaded.


15. HOW IT WORKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
User Flow:
1. User logs in/register -> initLoginForm/initRegisterForm
2. User uploads resume -> initFileUpload
3. User selects category -> loadSkills, initCategorySelect
4. User clicks Analyze -> analyzeResume
5. API simulated with skeleton loader
6. Data stored in localStorage
7. User redirected to result page
8. Result page reads localStorage and displays


